From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Henry <kevinhenry2027@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 17:47:53 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] g1_deploy: optional motor temperature warning and trip
 thresholds

The runtime already reads both motor temperatures (two sensors per motor) but only
warns, at a fixed 90 degC. Two optional thresholds act on each motor's
hotter reading, checked in CheckSafety() every control tick in
WAIT_FOR_CONTROL and CONTROL:

  --motor-temp-warn <degC>  print once per motor when it is reached
  --motor-temp-trip <degC>  stop control like the O key (damping, then exit)
                            and print which motor tripped

Both are off by default; SONIC's 90 degC audio/console warning is unchanged.
There is no softer "hold idle" level: the planner's idle is commanded through
the movement state the input thread owns, so overriding it from the control
loop would race the operator's input.
